From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winepulse: Keep open DualSense haptic PCM across Pulse churn

Opening the DualSense four-channel ALSA PCM directly can make PipeWire-Pulse
remove the corresponding sink while the raw handle owns the device.  The
Pulse subscription callback advances the global hotplug generation for that
expected removal, causing pulse_haptic_refresh_path() to reject the still-open
PCM before any haptic samples are written.

Treat the raw ALSA handle as authoritative once it has been opened.  Adopt the
new generation while the handle remains present, then let the existing PCM
state and write-error checks detect a real controller disconnect.  Those paths
still invalidate the old stream and never retarget it to another controller.
---
 dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
--- a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
+++ b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
@@ -2914,11 +2914,19 @@ static void pulse_haptic_invalidate(struct pulse_stream *stream, const char *rea
 
 static BOOL pulse_haptic_refresh_path(struct pulse_stream *stream)
 {
-    if (stream->haptic_pcm && stream->haptic_hotplug_generation == g_haptic_hotplug_generation)
-        return TRUE;
+    if (!stream->haptic_pcm)
+    {
+        TRACE("DualSense haptic stream has no open raw PCM.\n");
+        return FALSE;
+    }
 
-    TRACE("DualSense haptic stream no longer matches the current device generation.\n");
-    return FALSE;
+    if (stream->haptic_hotplug_generation != g_haptic_hotplug_generation)
+    {
+        TRACE("Keeping open DualSense haptic PCM across device generation %u -> %u.\n",
+                stream->haptic_hotplug_generation, g_haptic_hotplug_generation);
+        stream->haptic_hotplug_generation = g_haptic_hotplug_generation;
+    }
+    return TRUE;
 }
 
 static void pulse_haptic_advance(struct pulse_stream *stream, UINT32 frames, UINT32 frame_size)
